/* Accent flecks. The dissolve masks holes in the new-theme snapshot, and a
   background-image on that same pseudo-element paints in exactly those holes
   — so these colors only ever show through the dither band, never over solid
   page content.

   Four sparse checkerboards at coprime sizes, each a different category hue.
   Sizes are large relative to --dither-cell so only a small fraction of the
   knocked-out cells land on a colored patch; the rest fall on `transparent`
   and show the old theme underneath as usual.

   These read var(--portfolio-category-*), which are theme-conditional — and
   .dark has already toggled by the time this animates, so each hue resolves
   to the *destination* theme's value and stays legible against the
   background it's landing on. */
[data-theme-sweep-direction]::view-transition-new(root) {
  background-image:
    conic-gradient(
      var(--portfolio-category-art) 0 25%,
      transparent 25% 100%
    ),
    conic-gradient(
      var(--portfolio-category-games) 0 25%,
      transparent 25% 100%
    ),
    conic-gradient(
      var(--portfolio-category-creativity) 0 25%,
      transparent 25% 100%
